Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• event_name: to recognise installs (`first_open`) and un‑installs (`app_remove`).  
• event_timestamp: to measure the interval (micro‑seconds) between an install and the first uninstall.  
• event_date: to restrict the analysis to 2018‑08‑01 … 2018‑09‑30.  
• user_pseudo_id: anonymous device identifier – lets us treat one device as one “user”.  
• _TABLE_SUFFIX (BigQuery’s hidden meta‑column that appears when a wildcard is used): lets us pick only the August / September day‑tables.  

Typical filter / join conditions  

```
_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
AND event_name IN ('first_open','app_remove')
```

OR  

```
WHERE uninstall_ts IS NULL                                  -- never uninstalled
      OR uninstall_ts - first_open_ts > 7*24*60*60*1e6      -- uninstalled, but after 7 days
```



